  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ms Som Pan Products Pvt. Ltd. vs State Of Uttarakhand on 3 November, 2017 Author: Sudhanshu Dhulia Bench: Sudhanshu Dhulia In The High Court Of Uttarakhand At Nainital Criminal Misc. Application No.1469 of 2017 (under Section 482 Cr.P.C.) M/s Som Pan Products Private Limited ..........Applicant Versus State of Uttarakhand .........Respondent Hon'ble Sudhanshu Dhulia, J. (Oral) Mr. Sudhir Kumar, Advocate, present for the applicant. 2.",
    "facts": "3. A complaint has been filed by the respondent against the present applicant under Section 26 of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006, on which the learned Magistrate took cognizance in the matter and issued summon against the applicant. Aggrieved, the applicant preferred a revision before the revisional court, which was dismissed by the revisional court vide order dated 07.01.2016. Hence, the present application under Section 482 CrPC before this Court. 4. The applicant has been summoned under the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006. The applicant challenges the summoning order on various grounds, including the lack of jurisdiction.",
